   "question": "Design a first-order active low-pass filter with a cut-off frequency of 1 kHz and a pass-band gain of magnitude 2. Use C = 10 nF. Find R and the gain in dB at 10 kHz.",
   "steps": [
    "The cut-off formula gives R = 1/(2π f_c C).",
    "Substitute f_c = 1000 Hz and C = 10 nF = 10 × 10⁻⁹ F: R = 1/(2π × 1000 × 10 × 10⁻⁹) = 15.92 kΩ.",
    "The pass-band gain is 2. In decibels: 20 log10 2 = 6.02 dB, about 6 dB.",
    "At 10 kHz, f/f_c = 10. The magnitude is |H| = 2/√(1 + 10²) = 2/√101 = 0.199.",
    "In decibels: 20 log10 0.199 = −14.0 dB, or 6.02 − 20.04 = −14.02 dB."
   ],
