  {
   "level": "understand",
   "q": "Why does a first-order low-pass gain fall by 20 dB per decade above f_c?",
   "marks": 3,
   "a": "One RC section gives one pole. Above f_c the magnitude is approximately A0/(f/f_c), so the gain is inversely proportional to frequency. A tenfold increase in f divides the gain by 10, which is −20 dB."
  },
