   "level": "analyze",
   "q": "Explain why a summed low-pass plus high-pass does not by itself give a band-stop notch, and what is needed.",
   "marks": 4,
   "a": "At the crossover each first-order output is 0.707 of its pass-band value. Adding them gives about 1.414, a peak, not a zero. A band-stop needs the two paths to cancel at f0, so one path must be inverted before summing, or a twin-T network must be used."
